# Hidden files/dirs — strict policy: keep them out
.*
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
# Tier-4 4.4: CI workflows live under .github/ (hidden); explicit allow
!.github/
!.github/**

/vendor/*
/bin/*

# Archived documentation
/archive/

# Internal session/handoff documents (not for public release)
CLAUDE.md
*.scn.md
# …except the permanent contract primer, which is tracked alongside CONTRACT.md
!CONTRACT.scn.md
SESSION_*.md
MISSION_*.md
AUDIT_*.md

# Unit tests ARE tracked.
#
# They were not, and the exception list had reached three: the receipt vectors
# (the wire contract across four language implementations), the capability
# routing test (it decides which machine work goes to), and now schema
# resolution (it decides which dimension index a capability lands in). Each was
# argued individually as "not a test in the optional sense". At three, the rule
# is wrong rather than the exceptions: every test worth writing in a client
# library is about a contract with something it cannot see.
#
# Integration tests stay ignored — they need a live daemon and a populated
# ValKey, so they cannot run for anyone who checks this out.
/tests/Integration/

# Credentials and secrets
/.gnode/
/.env
*.password

# Cache files
/.phpunit.cache/
.claude/
*.bak
CLAUDE.md.bak
/demo/
/tools/benchmarks/
